WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
Welcome to our final topic in lesson four.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:06.840
How do you coach your player to be more agile

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.840
when you can't predict what's gonna happen next?

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.960
You don't coach for every scenario,

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.720
you coach for a mindset.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.640
This isn't just theory.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.240
In the sports world, speed, agility, quickness, training

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.400
is proven to boost an athlete's neuromuscular response

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.480
and decision-making speed.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.240
In the business world, the results are just as stark.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.120
A recent study found that high-agility organizations

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.400
had a 97% revenue growth

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:44.400
compared to just 46% for low-agility ones.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.000
Coaching for agility means empowering your player

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.320
to see change not as a threat,

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.680
but as an opportunity to pivot.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.200
Your role is to shift from being

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.840
the chief problem solver to the chief question asker,

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:04.600
building their capacity to adapt independently.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:08.960
A player was panicking because a key vendor

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.840
for her project pulled out.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.720
Her manager's first response wasn't, here's what we'll do.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.400
It was, okay, that's a tough break.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.200
What does this new constraint make possible?

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.040
That single question shifted the player from panic

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.640
to creative problem solving.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:31.680
Your play is to add one powerful agility question

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.680
to your coaching toolkit.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.680
The next time your player comes to you with a problem

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.240
or even delay in decision when conditions are in flux,

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.320
your first response will be,

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.080
what's your initial read on a path forward?

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.880
Your player's 90-day goal is suddenly at risk

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.360
due to a reorg.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.040
They come to you frustrated and ready to give up.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.040
How do you use agility coaching

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.600
to help them reframe the situation

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.120
and find a new way to win?

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.920
The agility coaching framework in your playbook

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.160
is designed for this exact scenario.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.240
Use it to structure a conversation that shifts your player

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.400
from frustration to creative problem solving.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.560
This completes lesson four.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:19.400
You are now equipped to activate your M.V.P. under pressure

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:22.400
and coach your team with greater agility.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.280
In our next lesson, Play the Season,

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.360
we will focus on sustaining this momentum

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:31.440
through energy management and course correction.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:32.440
I'll see you there.
